<div class="marketing-page" data-controller="scroll-reveal">
<%= render 'shared/navbar' %>

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="mkt-hero">
  <div class="mkt-inner" style="text-align: center;">
    <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; display: inline-flex;">
      <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow-dot"></span>
      Why Peponi.to exists
    </span>
    <h1 class="mkt-hero__title" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);">
      Why I built this
    </h1>
    <p class="mkt-hero__subtitle" style="margin: 0 auto;">
      I wanted a planner I would actually use. No subscription. No company sitting between me and my lists.
      This is the age of AI — anyone with a little grind can build this, or better. You can have mine.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Manifesto -->
<section class="mkt-section bg-white">
  <div class="mkt-inner--narrow">

    <div class="mkt-manifesto mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <div>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__icon bg-red-100 text-red-600">
          <%= inline_icon "gift" %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mkt-manifesto__title">Try it here. Keep it by running it.</h2>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__body">
          <p>peponi.to is a week on my server. Every theme, every view. Then I delete the account. If it isn’t useful, walk away. If it is, clone the repo and run it yourself. That is how you keep your lists.</p>
          <p>On <a href="https://omarchy.org/">Omarchy</a> you can skip the account entirely and keep tasks on that machine. That is what I use. After that, the day in front of you is the point. Write it down. Tick it off. Move on.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-manifesto mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <div>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__icon bg-orange-100 text-orange-600">
          <%= inline_icon "credit-card" %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mkt-manifesto__title">No subscription. No price tag.</h2>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__body">
          <p>£5 a month sounds like nothing until it’s £60 a year, and then you’ve bought the same app three times. That model is great for software companies. I don’t want to be one.</p>
          <p>This is MIT. Free. If you want sync, you run the server. If you want local-only, you run it on one machine. I am not billing you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-manifesto mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <div>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__icon bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-600">
          <%= inline_icon "building-storefront" %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mkt-manifesto__title">No app store</h2>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__body">
          <p>Thirty percent fees, months of review, sudden bans. Someone else always sits between you and the person who made the thing.</p>
          <p>The source is on GitHub. On Omarchy, a plugin on the bar. Unlike a paper planner, this one doesn’t run out of pages.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-manifesto mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <div>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__icon bg-green-100 text-green-600">
          <%= inline_icon "shield-check" %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mkt-manifesto__title">Yours to name</h2>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__body">
          <p>Click the title at the top of the planner and call the app whatever you like. Name your lists too. Put them at the bottom or on the right. Pick how many days you see (Today, or 2 through 7). Mix five themes, four fonts, eight colours. The defaults are a starting point, not a brand you have to live with.</p>
          <p>Export your data. Delete the account. On Omarchy, local mode never sends tasks to peponi.to. No ads, no streaks, no nudges. The only thing in front of you is the day.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-manifesto mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <div>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__icon bg-blue-100 text-blue-600">
          <%= inline_icon "device-phone-mobile" %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mkt-manifesto__title">A PWA that stays logged in</h2>
        <div class="mkt-manifesto__body">
          <p>After you buy, install it on your phone, tablet, or desktop. It stays signed in. Open it and you’re in. No constant re-login.</p>
          <p>No “Sign in with Google”. No Apple. No Facebook. Email and a password, with a remember-me if you want it. That’s the whole login.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- Philosophy -->
<section class="mkt-section mkt-section--cream">
  <div class="mkt-inner">
    <div class="mkt-section-intro mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
      <span class="mkt-label">What I care about</span>
      <h2 class="mkt-heading">Two simple bets</h2>
      <p class="mkt-subheading" style="margin: 0 auto;">
        These two ideas decide most of what I ship.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-grid-2" style="max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto;">

      <div class="mkt-philosophy mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item" style="--reveal-delay: 0ms">
        <div class="mkt-philosophy__quote">
          “Software should feel like owning a planner, not renting one.”
        </div>
        <div style="font-weight: 600; color: #4E5C64; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">Run it yourself</div>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">A week on my server, then gone</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">MIT, clone the repo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">Export or delete anytime</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">No payment</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mkt-philosophy mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="mkt-philosophy__quote">
          “The day in front of you is enough.”
        </div>
        <div style="font-weight: 600; color: #4E5C64; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">Keep it small</div>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">Today, or 2 through 7 days</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">Lists you name, parked for later</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">No notifications, no streaks</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center">
            <div class="hand-checkbox hand-checkbox-checked mr-3" style="transform: scale(0.8); flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
            <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4E5C64;">Rename the app if you want</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="mkt-cta mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">
  <div class="mkt-inner">
    <h2 class="mkt-cta__title">Try it for a week</h2>
    <p class="mkt-cta__subtitle">
      A week on my server. Then I delete it. Keep it by running it from source.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <%= link_to signup_path, class: "mkt-btn mkt-btn--white" do %>
        Try it here
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to github_source_url, class: "mkt-btn mkt-btn--ghost", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" do %>
        GitHub
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <p class="mkt-cta__trust">Made in Bolton, UK</p>
  </div>
</section>

<%= render 'shared/footer' %>
</div>
